        "original_id": "149c347a-b920-502b-aa70-afc2721469ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Carroll of Carrollton, Doc Watson\n- Places: Carroll County, Ohio, Homewood Field, San Diego, California\n- Topics: Declaration of Independence, Major League Baseball\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the last surviving signer of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the only Catholic signatory of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Carroll County, Ohio, was named for Charles Carroll of Carrollton.\n- Homewood Field and the entire campus took their names from the estate of Charles Carroll of Carrollton.\n- Doc Watson was born in Carroll County, Ohio, on January 30, 1886.\n- Doc Watson was a pitcher in Major League Baseball.\n- Doc Watson died in San Diego, California, on December 30, 1949.",
